This folder contains the full implementation of Part 1 of the project:
Evaluating the security of code using Static Analysis and Large Language Models (LLMs).

The framework performs:

1. Static Analysis of Python code using Bandit

2. LLM-based Security Evaluation via OpenAI GPT models

3. Comparison & Aggregation of both evaluations

4. Export of results to CSV for statistical analysis

Folder Structure
LLM evaluation/
├── part1_security_eval.py    # Main experiment driver
 ├── static_analysis.py        # Static analysis (Bandit)
 ├── llm_eval.py               # LLM-based security evaluator
 ├── utils.py                  # Shared dataclasses & types
 └── README

Installation:
Install all required packages:
pip install openai pandas bandit

Set your OpenAI API key:
bash: export OPENAI_API_KEY="your_api_key_here"

Dataset Format

Provide code samples as a JSONL file, one snippet per line:
{"id": "ex1", "source_type": "llm", "language": "python", "code": "def foo(x): return eval(x)"}
{"id": "ex2", "source_type": "authentic", "language": "python", "code": "def add(a,b): return a+b"}

Save as data.jsonl.

Running the Evaluation
Run the full evaluation pipeline:
python part1_security_eval.py --dataset data.jsonl --out results.csv




